BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c50cb22b-6768-408b-939b-143b03b24487@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T153300
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T170000
SUMMARY:Sun Rose
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Ecstatic / global dancefloor\n\nSince starting the Sun Rose pr
 oject in 2022\, Samu has been dedicated to bringing ecstatic ritual to th
 e dancefloor and celebrating resilience\, community\, and collaboration o
 n the decks. He has performed at Envision\, Dance Church\, Nectar\, Soar\
 , LIB\, the Castle in France\, Ohm in Berlin and the Soundgarden and Abra
 xas at Burning Man along with countless house parties and ecstatic dances
  around the globe.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/Samusunrose\nhttp://sound
 cloud.com/djsunrose/rythmeduchataeu\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival
 .com/products/sun-rose-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ec0807e1-9b14-4e66-96c5-6822ae08e930@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T183000
SUMMARY:Lili Rose
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Global / Batida / cumbia / Afro house • West Kootenay BC\n\n
 LiLi Rose is a DJ from the West Kootenay Region\, BC who plays mainly glo
 bal influenced electronic dance music. She plays genres like Batida\, new
  cumbia\, folktronica\, Latin club\, baile funk\, amapiano\, Afro house\,
  UK funky and more. A connoisseur of sound who loves to dance\, she has p
 layed stages such as Global Heat and Shambhala Music Festival and DJs ecs
 tatic dance events across British Columbia. Her collection is always grow
 ing and her style continually evolving as she searches out the freshest s
 ounds from around the world.\n\nhttp://soundcloud.com/lili-rose-23\nhttp:
 //instagram.com/lilis_creations_art/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestiva
 l.com/products/lili-rose
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9112ec55-8466-4548-83aa-593c4a4c4d24@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
SUMMARY:Sijay James
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:House / electronic • Nelson BC\n\nSijay James has been DJing
  since 1996 when he caught the vinyl bug in the earlier days of the Vanco
 uver electronic dance music scene. He has performed at venues around the 
 world and has been a strong part of the west coast festival community for
  nearly 3 decades. A resident of Nelson BC since 2008\, Sijay has also be
 en a creative force in the graphic design and art direction of numerous f
 estivals\, including a tenure as art director for Shambhala\, playing a l
 arge role in the development of dance music culture behind the scenes.\n\
 nhttps://soundcloud.com/onbeyond23\nhttps://www.instagram.com/onbeyond/\n
 \nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/sijay-james
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d7dff57e-4273-40ac-8400-0b9fc1fa08f3@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T213000
SUMMARY:Applecat
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Deep Dubstep / Fairytale Bass / Trap • West Coast Canada\n\n
 AppleCat is an internationally acclaimed DJ\, producer\, and vocalist fro
 m Canada’s West Coast\, known for blending Deep Dubstep\, Fairytale Bas
 s\, Trap\, and various world influences into cinematic\, grimy performanc
 es. Her sets feel less like a DJ set and more like a spell: bass-driven\,
  emotional\, and rooted in the belief that a revolution without dancing i
 s not a revolution worth having. Onstage she fuses live mashups\, reworks
 \, and ethereal vocals into hypnotic basslines. She has performed across 
 North America\, the UK\, and beyond\, including Burning Man\, Enchanted F
 orest Gathering\, Rifflandia\, Future Forest\, Evolve\, Envision\, and Ta
 ll Tree\, sharing lineups with CloZee\, Truth\, Emancipator\, Tipper\, Th
 e Polish Ambassador\, and The Halluci Nation. She was featured in the glo
 bal documentary Amplify Her (2017) and interviewed in DJ Mag.\n\nProfile:
  https://thenectarfestival.com/products/applecat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c06a25f5-efdf-4647-a21d-d9eb8e23aa5a@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T230000
SUMMARY:Kaya Ko
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Alt-folk / neo-soul / hip-hop / bass • vocalist\n\nKaya Ko i
 s a queer Filipinx vocalist & multi-media artist born on Turtle Island. T
 heir musical style blends alt-folk\, neo-RnB/Soul and HipHop with element
 s of West-coast Bass and EDM. A mix of classical training\, 12 years of s
 treet performance\, 20+ years of stage performances and self-teaching giv
 es Kaya an undeniable fluency. A gifted songwriter since age 10 and violi
 nist since age 5\, Kaya graduated from SAE Institute as an Electronic Mus
 ic Producer and Audio Engineer\, bringing soulful vocals and a rap style 
 reminiscent of influences like Lauryn Hill. A passionate member of the Fi
 lipinx community and advocate for marginalized voices\, Kaya offers a wid
 e spectrum from stripped-down acoustic and live looping to classic hip-ho
 p and RnB performance.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@kaya.ko_music\nhttps:/
 /www.instagram.com/kaya.ko.music/\nhttps://www.tiktok.com/@kaya.ko.music\
 nhttps://open.spotify.com/artist/2QZO5j7QLZMYVbyUeQhTDL\n\nProfile: https
 ://thenectarfestival.com/products/kaya-ko
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d3750cb8-ced4-476a-8cb8-2c9fe7a3fb99@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T003000
SUMMARY:Casey Club
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Garage / Dubstep / UK bass / DnB\n\nCasey Club is carving out 
 his own lane in the global bass music scene. Drawing from a deep understa
 nding of garage\, dubstep\, UK bass\, and drum & bass\, he delivers a sou
 nd that is unmistakably his own\, with sets packed with unreleased materi
 al that leave crowds asking for IDs. In 2025 he became a mainstay in the 
 Beatport Dubstep Top 5\, finishing the year as the 4th best-selling artis
 t on the platform\, with global support from Skrillex\, GRiZ\, Subtronics
 \, Four Tet\, Fred again..\, and Chase & Status\, and features on Deadbea
 ts\, UKF\, BBC Radio 1\, Rinse FM and SWU FM. Live highlights include a s
 tandout Shambhala debut and a sold-out run of Canadian headline shows\, p
 lus Boomtown and Love Saves The Day in the UK. 2026 brings his debut US/N
 orth American tour and an Australian tour.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/c
 aseyclubofficial/\nhttps://www.tiktok.com/@caseyclubofficial\nhttps://ope
 n.spotify.com/artist/2bmnpyZiHHOCrU988FwaJj\n\nProfile: https://thenectar
 festival.com/products/casey-club-and-snuffy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cbf6202e-4d38-4c80-ab00-8bb556024e59@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T003000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T020000
SUMMARY:Snuffy
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:140 / Bass / Breaks\n\nSnuffy is the solo project of an innova
 tive DJ and producer who has made a significant impact on the electronic 
 music scene with his dynamic sound\, rooted in 140 BPM and breaks. Fusing
  heavy basslines with vibrant\, dancefloor-ready energy\, his music bridg
 es the underground and mainstream with a blend of grit and groove\, drawi
 ng influence from trailblazers like Bakey\, Visages\, and Skream. With re
 leases on labels like Memory Palace\, Subsidia\, Odyzey\, Qualia\, and Bi
 te This\, and collaborations with EAZYBAKED\, PlayerDave\, JordnMoody and
  Snowy\, he has a rising presence on the U.S. festival circuit and a repu
 tation for electrifying live performances.\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/snuf
 fysounds\nhttps://open.spotify.com/artist/08yNyQvMaC3dLtOthzhPaZ\nhttps:/
 /www.instagram.com/snuffy.bass\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/
 products/snuffy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6e85259d-20af-495b-b82a-037947adb015@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T020000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T033000
SUMMARY:Entelechy
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Multi-genre electronic • West Coast\n\nActive in the West Co
 ast electronic music scene for over two decades\, Entelechy helped found 
 Returning Saturn events and artist collective\, and Ironic Spin sound cam
 p. Versed across many genres and settings\, from intimate living room gat
 herings to large multi-day festivals\, Entelechy plays for both dancers a
 nd listeners\, weaving a background of music theory\, composition\, arran
 gement\, and production with novel exploration of emerging styles\, frequ
 encies\, and harmonies. The term Entelechy describes the force within and
  around us that guides us to realize our inborn nature and manifest our h
 ighest potential.\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/entelechy\nhttps://www.instag
 ram.com/dj_entelechy/\nhttps://soundcloud.com/returning-saturn\n\nProfile
 : https://thenectarfestival.com/products/entelechy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b64bcd42-b696-455b-b8ee-f180c412c916@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T033000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T050000
SUMMARY:Dwam
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0c0ee29f-16dc-447c-99be-2e3f8c7411de@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T153300
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T170000
SUMMARY:The Moon Bodega
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Eclectic / bass • two decades DJing\n\nZain Burgess\, aka Mo
 on Bodega\, has been DJing for two decades. He saved up earnings from A&W
  at age 16 to afford a mixer and two turntables\, and has been obsessed e
 ver since. His sets are delicately engineered to activate the lightness a
 nd darkness — “bless your wounds\; that’s how the light gets in.”
 \n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/moon-bodega
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7f5c7204-3c13-41ad-8fd2-3cefe3293a6d@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T183000
SUMMARY:Khan
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Middle Eastern / House / Bass\n\nKhan is a seasoned DJ with de
 cades of experience behind the decks\, known for a unique sonic identity 
 that seamlessly blends Middle Eastern melodies with a diverse spectrum of
  House and Bass genres — from the pulsating depths of Deep Dubstep to t
 he infectious grooves of Trance\, Progressive\, Funky\, Deep\, and Bass H
 ouse.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/khan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:06277fc9-b84f-441d-a374-5a75dd1997f0@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T200000
SUMMARY:Rah
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Eclectic • South Okanagan / West Coast\n\nRAH aka Noradawn h
 as a nomadic spirit\, having lived many places. Born in Alberta\, she spe
 nt part of her childhood in Florida and Colombia\, South America. She cur
 rently lives in a forest on the edge of the South Okanagan Valley and spl
 its her time between there and the west coast.\n\nProfile: https://thenec
 tarfestival.com/products/rah
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:493e7e5e-0609-4f97-aca9-4232907af799@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T213000
SUMMARY:Aninja
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Drum & Bass • Vancouver\n\nRyan Halston AKA ANiNjA is a Drum
  and Bass Producer/DJ from Vancouver\, Canada. His style focuses on blend
 ing deep minimal rollers with a healthy selection of MCs and vocalists. W
 ith over 20 years of making music under his belt\, his sound selection is
  sure to get the attention of a crowd. Ryan began DJing in 2013\, origina
 lly as a Hip Hop DJ/producer/MC known as SkyWryter hosting local shows in
  the Okanagan. In 2020 his style shifted to Drum and Bass and he moved to
  Vancouver in 2021 where he has been active in the underground scene. Man
 y of ANiNjA's sets are packed with his original music plus exclusive trac
 ks and dubs\, bringing underground UK DnB sounds to Canada. He has also b
 een a sound engineer since 2012\, currently the primary sound tech at Red
  Room Vancouver for Subculture Saturdays.\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/aninj
 amusic\nhttps://www.instagram.com/aninja_dj\nhttps://www.youtube.com/@ani
 nja_dj\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/aninja
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ae687f55-2435-4978-9f03-610be5befbf4@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T223000
SUMMARY:Kytami x Gospel of Her
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Live violin / DnB / bass\n\nThere are few acts on the west coa
 st combining live instrumentation\, high energy and gritty bass music wit
 h the ferocity and craft of violinist Kytami. She has made it her mission
  to create a truly unique\, instantly recognizable sound\, drawing on her
  love of Drum n Bass\, Hip Hop and more — here joined by Gospel of Her.
 \n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/kytami
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:741c65c4-35b3-4b9b-b178-b78ac7ffc078@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T223000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T000000
SUMMARY:Mirage
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:140 / Breaks / Jungle / DnB\n\nMirage’s musical journey mirr
 ors the illusory nature of sound\, bending and refracting across genres t
 o create an experience that captivates and transcends expectations. Mirag
 e immerses himself in the depths of 140\, Breaks\, Jungle and Drum & Bass
 \, consistently pushing the boundaries.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfest
 ival.com/products/mirage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cf51e41b-2d69-4b54-97f1-d7e0394ea39c@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T013000
SUMMARY:Mazeguider
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Genre-fluid / journey sets\n\nThe Mazeguider brings a singular
  sensibility to the decks\, weaving journeys full of emotional power\, co
 mpelling sounds\, and undeniable grooves. The genre may mutate as freshne
 ss and novelty shift through different sounds and styles\, but it’s all
  driven by a beacon that beckons us forward on each step.\n\nProfile: htt
 ps://thenectarfestival.com/products/mazeguider
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4ec55e4a-d161-44d7-a3de-395bfe08d4d3@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T013000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T030000
SUMMARY:Kilbourne
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Sound system / bass • Anishinaabe\, Sunshine Coast\n\nEmergi
 ng from the coastal rainforests of British Columbia’s Sunshine Coast an
 d Gulf Islands comes Anishinaabe First Nations artist Kilbourne\, founder
  and curator of Cimmerian Records. Kilbourne channels a sound resonating 
 on deep foundations\, crafting a sonic narrative deeply rooted in sound s
 ystem culture.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/kilbour
 ne
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a737d135-4f6c-41a8-af65-99eab709e255@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T030000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T043000
SUMMARY:Grey Moon
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Genre-fluid • Kootenay\n\nGrey Moon is a Kootenay-based\, ge
 nre-fluid artist known for eclectic yet cohesive sets. With inclusivity a
 s ethos\, there’s a little something for everyone in their journey. He 
 is half of Swoon with Alex Moon — a collaboration of love\, lust and lo
 ss.\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/greymoonmusic\n\nProfile: https://thenectar
 festival.com/products/grey-moon
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:90434bbe-a2d0-432e-88b2-544b31b3c7c9@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T043000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T060000
SUMMARY:Sundog
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Turntablist / hip-hop / bass • Victoria\n\nVictoria-based tu
 rntablist and producer. Combining the original styles of old school hip-h
 op with low end bass music makes for dope beats and heavy drops with a li
 ttle taste of nostalgia.\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/officialsundog\n\nProf
 ile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/sundog
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ed6571af-d58e-4b45-a58e-b60717c476dc@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T123000
SUMMARY:Unity Partner Massage (Susan Horning)
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f111fff7-6364-4211-bb1c-555deb9010b4@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T140000
SUMMARY:Meditative Musical Sound Journey (Andrew Kim)
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e9cb39a0-328c-4a5d-b1a2-dd2f1d6bf822@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T213000
SUMMARY:J2
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Global club / breaks / dancehall • Victoria\n\nJ² is Den an
 d BB Stepz\, a Victoria-based DJ duo rooted in BC’s festival and underg
 round music culture. Their sets are bass-forward and rhythm-driven\, draw
 ing on global club sounds and blending polyrhythmic percussion\, moody me
 lodies\, vocal textures\, and low-end weight. They move through global cl
 ub\, breaks\, dancehall and more.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.c
 om/products/bb-stepz
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7740ab13-805b-418e-93a8-4d79d70eb76f@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T230000
SUMMARY:J.F.Killah
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Deep / dark bass\n\nWith a love for the underground and an aff
 inity for deep\, dark\, grimy basslines\, J.F.Killah has a passion for en
 gaging dance floors worldwide. She has graced the decks in Canada\, Europ
 e\, New Zealand\, United States\, and Central America\, and performed at 
 festivals including Shambhala\, Bass Coast\, Electric Love\, and Riffland
 ia.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/jf-killah
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1a8c7837-99bd-42a7-8944-9c4a665efb0c@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T001500
SUMMARY:Stage Closed
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cf6f7329-aaf3-43cf-8b51-c9df5c90e818@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T003000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T013000
SUMMARY:Abstrakt Sonance & The Nectar Orchestra
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Live immersive multimedia premiere\n\nSomething truly special 
 is being created for Nectar 2026: the live immersive multimedia debut of 
 Abstrakt Sonance & The Nectar Orchestra\, featuring Kytami\, Sosita\, Rob
  Christian\, Marshall Rasmussen\, Lady of the Mist\, Dredekop\, Doug Gork
 off\, Liesl Petersen\, and Tomemos.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival
 .com/products/abstrakt-sonance-the-nectar-orchestra
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7bb8e726-6ac9-4318-bec5-7e53ff286f71@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T013000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T030000
SUMMARY:Saturna
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Ethereal beats / soundscapes • Sunshine Coast\n\nOriginating
  from the Sunshine Coast\, British Columbia\, ethereal beatsmith Saturna 
 has an artistic voice unlike any other. By drawing inspiration from a ple
 thora of sources\, Saturna has crafted a stirring and enigmatic productio
 n style that blends meticulously carved soundscapes with irresistible gro
 oves.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/saturna
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b891dc5a-25fc-4a81-9118-5ec5a1ec8f41@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T030000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T050000
SUMMARY:Leland River
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Eclectic / festival • North West Coast\n\nA North-Westcoast 
 fixture\, Leland River is a DJ/Producer whose growth as an artist and hum
 an being is deeply tied to the mycelial webs of the BC festival scene. He
  is trusted by many of his peers and listeners for his diverse array of p
 roductions\, mixes\, and adept sense for playing the right music at the r
 ight time.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/leland-river
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b2c75c0e-5805-4b31-b4e4-510d9ec8449b@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T050000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T063000
SUMMARY:Melo.Nade
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Hip-hop / crate-digging • Calgary\n\nNavin ‘Melo.Nade’ H
 uq was born and raised in Calgary\, Canada. Growing up with hip-hop cultu
 rists\, he learned the art of digging at an early age\, resulting in an i
 nsatiable addiction for finding hard-to-find gems. As a child he spent ti
 me recording mix tapes off the radio\, TV\, and beyond.\n\nProfile: https
 ://thenectarfestival.com/products/melo-nade
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3274405d-cf98-4a5f-ac2a-7af7465b0112@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T063000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T080800
SUMMARY:Okiro
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Dubstep / garage / grime / R&B • West Coast\n\nGrowing up on
  the West Coast of Canada\, Okiro was shaped by BC’s thriving festival 
 culture\, which sparked his passion for music from an early age. Blending
  sub-heavy dubstep\, garage\, grime\, rap\, and R&B\, Okiro’s sound is 
 both an ode to the UK’s underground bass scene and a reflection of more
  melodic influences.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/o
 kiro
END:VEVENT
